# Aviation Device Lifecycle Management System

## 📌 Project Overview  
Designed and implemented a centralized operational management system to track and manage the lifecycle of onboard aviation devices — from manufacturing to regulatory clearance and aircraft installation.

## 🎯 Problem Statement  
Operational tracking processes were fragmented across spreadsheets and email chains, leading to delays, accountability issues, and poor cross-functional coordination among hardware, finance, customs, and customer success teams.

## 🛠️ Solution Approach  
- Developed a structured issue management and tracking platform using **Jira Software** with tailored workflows and SLA mechanisms.
- Replaced spreadsheets with dynamic digital dashboards and standardized reporting templates.
- Established escalation protocols, agile stand-ups, and periodic action plan reviews for proactive issue handling.
- Integrated notification systems to ensure on-time delivery and operational visibility.

## 📊 Results & Impact  
- Reduced operational delivery delays by **19%** in the first operational year.
- Achieved full transparency in asset and delivery management processes.
- Increased cross-functional accountability, improving operational readiness and customer satisfaction.

## 🔧 Tech Stack  
- Jira Software  
- Grafana  
- Confluence  
- Google Workspace  
- Slack API  

## 📈 Key Takeaways  
A data-driven operational framework drastically improves coordination and transparency in complex, multi-stakeholder environments like aviation tech deployments.
